@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+requires "reference-semantics/semantics.k"
+
+module VERIFICATION-BODY-MUTANT
+  imports MPY
+
+  // Operational-sensitivity mutant: the submitted len call is replaced by 0.
+  syntax Module ::= "strlenModuleMutant" [macro]
+  rule strlenModuleMutant
+    => Module(
+         FuncDef(
+           "strlen",
+           Params("string"),
+           Return(Int(0))
+         )
+       )
+
+  syntax KItem ::= "#invokeStrlenMutant" "(" Val ")"
+  rule <k> #invokeStrlenMutant(V:Val)
+        => #loadAll(strlenModuleMutant) ~> Call(Name("strlen"), V) ... </k>
+endmodule

codex
The mutation gates behaved correctly. The off-by-one postcondition parsed and dry-ran successfully, then failed with exit 1 on the expected residual `isLen(S) + 1 = isLen(S)`; the empty string is a concrete counterexample. A separate body-sensitivity mutant replacing `return len(string)` with `return 0` also built and failed on `0 = isLen(S)`, showing the successful proof depends on the submitted body rather than an oracle or bypass.
Adequacy, exhaustive source inventory, non-vacuity, and independent body-sensitivity checks are complete. The remaining work is to consolidate the trust ledger and evidence into REVIEW.md and validate the required terminal markers.
